  "worked_solution": "The condition after the \"$:$\" symbol\n\n$$\nn\\in N,\\,n\\ge 2\n$$\n\nstates that $n$ can be any natural number that satisfies the inequality $n\\ge 2.$ In other words, \n\n$$\nn={2,3,4,5,\u2026}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elements of $A$ are all the terms of the sequence ${a}_{n},$ given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}={n}^{2}+2n,\\,n\\in {2,3,4,5,\u2026}.\n$$\n\nLet's write down the first few terms of our sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{2} & ={2}^{2}+2(2)=4+4=8 \\\\ {a}_{3} & ={3}^{2}+2(3)=9+6=15 \\\\ {a}_{4} & ={4}^{2}+2(4)=16+8=24 \\\\ {a}_{5} & ={5}^{2}+2(5)=25+10=35 \\\\  & \u22ee\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\nA={8,15,24,35,\u2026}.\n$$",
